{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1459139-need-some-help-making-my-mage-well-mage-y","id":1459139,"title":"Need some help making my mage, well, mage-y","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-09-07T08:47:09-07:00","id":1459139,"title":"Need some help making my mage, well, mage-y","content":"Okay so my group just started playing a game of mage 20th, using the core book and tome of secrets. While I have a decent idea how the game works (better than the rest of the group, barring the ST), I still have some problems comprehending how some things work. I would appreciate some help if that's at all possible! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> First off, My character is a Taftani war veteran (game is set in 1998), and he's basically living his life on medical discharge/GI bill/whatnot while working part-time at a local detective agency. He was a motorpool mechanic in the army, so he wasn't seriously into combat or anything, more working on engines and stuff. He is a mystic mage, not a technocrat, mostly because his years growing up learning cars included all those little superstitions and ritual behavior that just seemed to 'work right'. His practice is Shamanism, with an urban bend, and his 7 implements are: Artwork, Household tools, Books-scrolls-periodicals, brews-potions-powders, circles-pentacles-geometric designs, weapons, and offerings-sacrifices. My Spheres are Matter 3, Prime 2, Spirit 2, and Forces 1<br /> <br /> We're only like 3 game sessions in, and we're investigating a local street racing scene, since one of the racers recently awakened and was using his newfound abilities to 'trick out' his car to be way more powerful, etc. The problem is that he's not only skipped out on his family (who is paying us to find him) but also has been stealing from other mages in our chantry (which is also paying us to return the stolen items/capture the thief). The point of this is that my character is a decent driver and has volunteered to take part in the next race so he can chase the kid down.<br /> <br /> The problem is that I don't quite grasp how making spells as tools or weapons work. Like, say I want to 'soup up' my car so that I have a bunch of different effects, what exactly would that process entail? Like, how does casting a spell using my car work? I know mechanically if I was driving it and wanted to say, make the tires impenetrable so I could run over spike strips or something, I should be able to cast it from a dice perspective, but how do I make it work? Do I spend the time working on the car in advance to prepare the tires and cast the spell as a ritual? How long would that last? I have a number of different implements that I could use, but what if I wanted to work in multiple effects into the car at the same time?<br /> <br /> In case there's further questions, here's what he wants to do with the car:<br /> *Armor it to prevent it from being busted up in case he drives into someone or something.<br /> *Attach a spirit to the car to assist his driving skills<br /> *Reinforce the tires to prevent blow-outs<br /> *Keep the car fueled with gas and NOS<br /> <br /> I'm aware that with Forces 1 I can't do any of those effects, which is why I was going for more of a 'make the car able to handle being pushed harder than it ever could' approach.<br /> <br /> I'm still not sure how casting spells with weapons works either. For example, if a mirrorshades has a plasma rifle, do they make a spell roll every time they pull the trigger, or do they make the spell when the item is crafted? What about issued weaponry? I'm just trying to wrap my head around this and I feel like I'm just a wee bit away from having a eureka moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T11:35:38-07:00","id":1459161,"title":"","content":"You aren't casting a spells using your car so much as casting a spells on your car. What is happening depends a lot on what you are trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> For your example of on the fly casting to reinforce the tires there are several ways your character might accomplish this. A sacrifice would work. Your character might also have worked the proper geometric designs into his hubcaps and he could use those as his focus. You can actually presume that your character has done a lot of setup work for his spells in his off time, so this is perfectly fine.<br /> <br /> On the other hand your character could actually spend the time doing a ritual to reinforce the tires. This might take the the form of carving designs into the hubcaps, reading from various arcane tomes, or brewing up some kind of potion/coating.<br /> <br /> Now I did put carving a design into both categories and that was intentional. To a bystander it might seem like the same thing is going on but the effects are quite different mechanically. In the first case, the character is just putting his focus into a position where he can easily use it. He'll have to make the magic roll when he casts the spell and nothing stops him from casting it again when he needs to. In the case of the ritual, the design is a part of the casting and the spell is already in effect when the race starts. He's not going to be able to cast the spell again if he needs to, either, at least not as a ritual.<br /> <br /> As for Mirrorshades, if the weapon is his focus he is essentially casting a new spell ever time. On the other hand the weapon might be a Wonder and would follow the rules for Wonders. There's a third option, which isn't all that likely but possible. With the use of Time a spell can be left hanging: already cast but waiting until the trigger to fire. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":758,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","user":"Ramnesis","date":". 09-07-2021, 02:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T11:50:34-07:00","id":1459165,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1459139-need-some-help-making-my-mage-well-mage-y?p=1459161#post1459161\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You aren't casting a spells using your car so much as casting a spells on your car. What is happening depends a lot on what you are trying to accomplish.<br /> <br /> On the other hand your character could actually spend the time doing a ritual to reinforce the tires. This might take the the form of carving designs into the hubcaps, reading from various arcane tomes, or brewing up some kind of potion/coating.<br /> <br /> In the case of the ritual, the design is a part of the casting and the spell is already in effect when the race starts. He's not going to be able to cast the spell again if he needs to, either, at least not as a ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay these are the snippets of what I was feeling but wasn't sure how I should approach executing it. Yeah, my character's car is one he's had since he awakened, and he's done 'restoration' work on it in the background and as part of his history. I think the act of doing rituals to cast spells on the car would work well. Would I need time magic to make the ritual effect last a long time (days), or does prime handle that part?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T12:06:01-07:00","id":1459167,"title":"","content":"Duration is a usually determined by successes. The number needed is on the damage and duration chart. You won't need Time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T12:40:10-07:00","id":1459171,"title":"","content":"Okay thanks, I need to go find that chart; cause I totally absolutely know what I'm doing! (no I don't)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T18:29:15-07:00","id":1459226,"title":"","content":"There is one thing I have not found the answer to. If a Mage has multiple ways of improving something, he should be able to improve it More than if he had only one way. A Mage with Prime 2 can enchant a car or an essential part like the engine. With Matter 3, you can improve it by refining its shape or density. With Matter 2 and Spirit 2, he can imbue it with ephemeral power. Rungoc's character has all of these. For the purpose of armoring the car, he should be able to use all three on the body of the car to make it practically impenetrable (in the case of Spirit, using that of a turtle). Is there a limit to the number ways an object can be improved by Magick?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-07T19:16:53-07:00","id":1459236,"title":"","content":"I can't remember the exact rule out of my mind right now, but there is. A single Pattern will become saturated at a certain point, based on the number of simultaneous effects on it. This can lead to effects similar to Pattern Bleeding, increased difficulty on casting new effects on it, among others. But I can't reach the book right now to get the precise rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T04:57:29-07:00","id":1459278,"title":"","content":"I remember that, I also remember something about similar spells not stacking. In the case of several armor spells, only the most effective one applies. I can't find either one in a quick skim of M20, and I think at least one of them is actually from Mage the Awakening, but I don't know which.<br /> <br /> There is a rule about increasing difficulties for maintaining too many effects at once, but that only applies to effects that you have to concentrate to maintain, not effects with a duration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-09-08T07:31:33-07:00","id":1459300,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1459139-need-some-help-making-my-mage-well-mage-y?p=1459278#post1459278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I remember that, I also remember something about similar spells not stacking. In the case of several armor spells, only the most effective one applies. I can't find either one in a quick skim of M20, and I think at least one of them is actually from Mage the Awakening, but I don't know which.<br /> <br /> There is a rule about increasing difficulties for maintaining too many effects at once, but that only applies to effects that you have to concentrate to maintain, not effects with a duration.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Good to know! This discussion actually helped me figure out a way to get around the tires issue: They're enchanted to maintain at least a certain amount of air in them, regenerating air if they fall low. I think I can do that with matter, so it actually works to make sure there aren't any stacking effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1401-rungok","name":"rungok","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1401_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"141"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}